      "name": "is_high_frequency_topic",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.45,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "rationale": "Largely redundant with 'topic'—it is a derived binary threshold on topic frequency, offering limited new leverage. Values are consistent with topic assignments (rare Printer=No, common VPN/Database=Yes), so grounding is fine."
    },
    {
      "name": "attention_flag",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "rationale": "A prioritization/anomaly signal directly matches the query's intent. However, the basis for High/Medium/Low-Anomaly is not clearly derivable from the sampled source text: e.g. 'Unable to access online database' flagged Medium while similar VPN/WiFi issues are Routine, with no textual justification, suggesting partly invented severity beyond available evidence."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.8,
  "rationale": "The 'topic' column is a genuinely useful, well-grounded categorization for triaging incidents. 'attention_flag' targets the query's core need but its severity distinctions are only partially supported by the visible source text. 'is_high_frequency_topic' is grounded but adds little beyond 'topic'. Overall the added set provides real analytical leverage with moderate grounding concerns on the flag."
}

